From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: take the N-PHY TX I/Q LO results out instead of overwriting them

At the end of b43_nphy_cal_tx_iq_lo() the calibration engine has left its
result in the IQLOCAL table at offset 96, and the driver is meant to read
it from there and install it at offset 80, where the rest of the driver
looks for the coefficients. The two calls have their direction swapped:

	b43_ntab_write_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 96), 4, buffer);
	b43_ntab_read_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 80), 4, buffer);

So the driver overwrites the engine's result at 96 with the stale
contents of buffer, then reads offset 80 into buffer instead of writing
it. Offset 80 keeps whatever it had, and what the calibration produced is
destroyed by the write that was supposed to collect it. The three pairs
that follow in the same block are the right way round, which is what
makes this look like a transcription slip rather than intent.

The reference reads 96 and writes 80:

	wlc_phy_table_read_nphy(pi, NPHY_TBL_ID_IQLOCAL, 4, 96, 16, tbl_buf);
	wlc_phy_table_write_nphy(pi, NPHY_TBL_ID_IQLOCAL, 4, 80, 16, tbl_buf);

An MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362 (N-PHY rev 8, radio 2057
rev 8) writes four words to offset 80 at the end of the calibration, and
the first is 0x0059. Before this change the driver never writes offset 80
there at all, so the transmit power control coefficient setup that reads
it later computes from zeros; after it, offset 80 carries 0x0059 as in
the capture, and the matched operations over the calibration rise from
1195 of 1570 to 1308.

This is not specific to radio 2057 rev 8: the block is shared by every
N-PHY rev 3 and later, so it is deliberately not gated.

Verified: record #10640, "TBL.WR   id=0x000f off=0x0050 len=4"
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/d2c490d/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n25914

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
index 22359bd9d..56cf3ee25 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -5499,8 +5499,8 @@ static int b43_nphy_cal_tx_iq_lo(struct b43_wldev *dev,
 		last = (dev->phy.rev < 3) ? 6 : 7;
 
 		if (!mphase || nphy->mphase_cal_phase_id == last) {
-			b43_ntab_write_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 96), 4, buffer);
-			b43_ntab_read_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 80), 4, buffer);
+			b43_ntab_read_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 96), 4, buffer);
+			b43_ntab_write_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 80), 4, buffer);
 			if (dev->phy.rev < 3) {
 				buffer[0] = 0;
 				buffer[1] = 0;
